Not necessarily. A lujvo means what the lujvo maker makes it mean once you
define its structure, so it's a matter of agreeing on the meaning, there's
no right or wrong. For {mutce} I use {-tce} but for {mleca} I prefer
{mec-}.

Of course I've no problem with {rodme'a} as {ko'a mleca ko'e lo ka broda
kei ko'i} but it has exactly the same sumti places as {mecybo'e} (as
defined in my previous message).

